l("fop","End_C(V)","S002","S002","arbitrary","Consider arbitrary complex-linear endomorphism fop.",["V"]),
l("gop","End_C(V)","S002","S002","arbitrary","Consider arbitrary complex-linear endomorphism gop.",["V"]),
l("Q_C","End_C(V)","S003","S006","definition","Put Q_C=Y(ell)X(ell).",["Y","X","ell","V"]),
l("A_C","family Fin(n)×Fin(n)→End_C(V)","S004","S006","definition","Put A_C_ij=X(ell−i)Q_C Y(ell−j).",["X","Y","ell","Q_C","n","V"])
],argument:[
s("S001","By H007 every X_r,Y_r preserves M, so its restriction is a Z-linear endomorphism. Inclusion M→V is injective because M is a submodule. The original complex identities r!X_r=x^r and r!Y_r=y^r therefore restrict to r!X_M(r)=x_M^r and r!Y_M(r)=y_M^r for every r≥0. These are identities using integer multiples of operators, with no division in M. By H005, h=xy−yx, so h preserves M and restricts to h_M=x_M y_M−y_M x_M. The inclusions intertwine x_M,y_M,h_M with x,y,h.",["H005","H007"],[],["M","V","X","Y","X_M","Y_M","x_M","y_M","h_M","x","y","h"],[f("F001","For every natural r, r!X_M(r)=x_M^r and r!Y_M(r)=y_M^r; inclusion M→V is injective and intertwines x_M,y_M,h_M with x,y,h.",["M","V","X_M","Y_M","x_M","y_M","h_M","x","y","h"],[["r","natural number"]])]),
s("S002","N001 supplies the complex basis e. Define its coordinate endomorphisms E_ij by E_ij e_k=delta_(j,k)e_i. They exist by linear extension on a basis. To record how operator equalities will be checked, fix arbitrary complex endomorphisms fop,gop and temporarily assume L1 that they agree on each e_i. M007, with scalar homomorphism Id_C, yields fop=gop. Discharging L1 and quantifying these maps gives: any two complex-linear endomorphisms agreeing on every e_i are equal.",["N001","M007"],[],["V","e","n","E","fop","gop"],[f("F002","For any two complex-linear endomorphisms of V, agreement on every e_i implies equality.",["V","e"])],["L1"],["L1"]),
s("S003","Put Q_C=Y_ell X_ell. The N001 divided-power formulas show X_ell kills e_k for k<ell and sends e_ell to e_0, while Y_ell e_0=e_ell. Thus Q_C=E_(ell,ell), by F002. They also give X_(ell−i)e_ell=e_i (its binomial coefficient is choose(ell−i,ell−i)=1), so X_(ell−i)Q_C=E_(i,ell) for every i. All formulas include ell=0.",["N001"],["F002"],["Q_C","X","Y","ell","e","n","E"],[f("F003","Q_C=E_(ell,ell) and, for every i∈Fin(n), X_(ell−i)Q_C=E_(i,ell).",["Q_C","E","ell","X","n"],[["i","Fin(n)"]])]),
s("S004","Put A_C_ij=X_(ell−i)Q_C Y_(ell−j). On e_k, if k<j the vector Y_(ell−j)e_k has index below ell and is killed by Q_C; if k>j it goes past the top index and is already zero. For k=j it is choose(ell,ell−j)e_ell. M004 at (ell,j) and (ell,ell−j) gives choose(ell,j) j!(ell−j)!=ell!=choose(ell,ell−j)(ell−j)!j!. Cancel the nonzero integer factorial product to obtain choose(ell,ell−j)=choose(ell,j)=c_j. Hence Q_C Y_(ell−j)=c_j E_(ell,j), and F003 gives A_C_ij=c_j E_ij. In each instance equality on every basis vector is promoted to equality of endomorphisms by F002.",["N001","M004"],["F002","F003"],["A_C","Q_C","X","Y","ell","e","n","E","c"],[f("F004","For every i,j∈Fin(n), Q_C Y_(ell−j)=c_j E_(ell,j) and A_C_ij=c_j E_ij.",["Q_C","Y","ell","c","E","A_C","n"],[["i","Fin(n)"],["j","Fin(n)"]])]),
s("S005","On every basis vector, E_ij E_kl equals E_il if j=k and 0 otherwise; F002 proves the operator identity. By F004, A_C_ij A_C_kl=c_j A_C_il if j=k (both sides are c_j c_l E_il), and 0 otherwise. By definition d_j c_j=Dprod, also for the singleton index set. Acting on e_k gives (∑_j d_j A_C_jj)e_k=Dprod e_k. F002 therefore gives ∑_j d_j A_C_jj=Dprod Id_V.",[],["F002","F004"],["E","A_C","c","d","Dprod","e","n","V"],[f("F005","For i,j,k,l∈Fin(n), A_C_ij A_C_kl=c_j A_C_il when j=k and 0 otherwise; d_j c_j=Dprod; ∑_j d_j A_C_jj=Dprod Id_V.",["A_C","c","d","Dprod","n","V"],[["i","Fin(n)"],["j","Fin(n)"],["k","Fin(n)"],["l","Fin(n)"]])]),
s("S006","The products defining Q_M,A_ij are restrictions of Q_C,A_C_ij, since all their divided-power factors preserve M. Thus all coefficients and operators in F005 preserve M, and composition with the injective inclusion M→V transfers each identity to End_Z(M): A_ij A_kl=c_j A_il for j=k and 0 otherwise, and ∑_j d_j A_jj=Dprod Id_M. Along with d_j c_j=Dprod and F001 this is N002. Only c_j E_ij is asserted to preserve M over Z.",["H007"],["F001","F005"],["M","V","Q_M","Q_C","A","A_C","c","d","Dprod","X_M","Y_M","x_M","y_M","h_M","E","n"])
],applications:[
ap("M007","S002","R0=R1=C, sigma=Id_C, M0=M1=V, I0=Fin(n), b0=e, f1=fop, f2=gop.",["N001 gives the e-basis and fop,gop are arbitrary C-linear endomorphisms (Id_C-semilinear maps).","The temporary premise L1 is precisely equality of fop,gop on every e_i."]),
ap("M004","S004","n0=ell, j0=j for arbitrary j∈Fin(n).",["j∈Fin(ell+1), so j≤ell."],"A001"),
ap("M004","S004","n0=ell, j0=ell−j for the same j.",["0≤ell−j≤ell by j≤ell."],"A002")
]});
rs.push({id:"R003",inputs:["H003","H004","H007","M002","M005","M008","M009","E001"],output:"N003",definitions:["D001","D002","D005","D006","D007","D020","D021","D022","D025"],rules:["direct","exists_elimination","forall_introduction"],locals:[
