rs.push({id:"R004",inputs:["H001","H002","H003","H007","N002","N003","M003","M004"],output:"N004",definitions:["D001","D002","D007","D008","D010","D011","D012","D013","D014","D015","D016","D017","D018","D019","D020","D023","D024"],rules:["direct","forall_introduction","implication_introduction","natural_induction"],locals:[
l("j","Fin(n)","S001","S002","arbitrary","Fix an arbitrary index j.",["n"]),
l("i","Fin(n)","S002","S002","arbitrary","Fix an arbitrary index i in the multiplication calculation.",["n"]),
l("k","Fin(n)","S002","S002","arbitrary","Fix an arbitrary index k.",["n"]),
l("lidx","Fin(n)","S002","S002","arbitrary","Fix an arbitrary fourth index lidx (written l in formulas).",["n"]),
l("r","natural number","S003","S003","arbitrary","Fix an arbitrary natural r for the conditional assertion r≤ell.",[]),
l("W","K-linear subspace of U","S004","S004","arbitrary","Let W be an arbitrary K-linear subspace of U.",["K","U"])
],argument:[
s("S001","H003 gives lambda=(ell:Z) and ell<p. Since p is prime and char K=p (H001,H002), M003 at r0=ell gives that red(ell!) is a unit, hence nonzero in the field K. For j∈Fin(n), M004 at (ell,j) gives c_j j!(ell−j)!=ell!. After applying red this is red(c_j) red(j!) red((ell−j)!)=red(ell!)≠0. No factor of a nonzero product in a field can be zero, so red(c_j)≠0 for every j. The finite product red(Dprod)=∏_j red(c_j) is nonzero.",["H001","H002","H003","M003","M004"],[],["p","K","lambda","ell","n","j","c","red","Dprod"],[f("F001","For every j∈Fin(n), red(c_j)≠0; also red(Dprod)≠0.",["n","red","c","Dprod"])]),
s("S002","Use the ring-homomorphism laws of F from N003 on N002. Integer multiples of an endomorphism become scalar multiples by their image in K: repeated addition and negation commute with F. Scalars commute with K-linear maps. When j≠k, the integer multiplication identity gives T_ij T_k,lidx=0. When j=k it gives T_ij T_j,lidx=red(c_j)^(-1)red(c_lidx)^(-1)F(c_j A_i,lidx)=red(c_lidx)^(-1)F(A_i,lidx)=T_i,lidx. Cancellation uses F001. The sum identity becomes ∑_j red(d_j)F(A_jj)=red(Dprod)Id_U. From d_j c_j=Dprod and F001, red(d_j)=red(Dprod)red(c_j)^(-1); divide the sum identity by the nonzero red(Dprod) to get ∑_j T_jj=Id_U. These are endomorphism identities on U; no reduction of the characteristic-zero e-basis has been presumed.",["H007","N002","N003"],["F001"],["F","T","A","c","d","Dprod","red","U","K","i","j","k","lidx","n"],[f("F002","For all i,j,k,l∈Fin(n), T_ij T_kl equals T_il when j=k and 0 otherwise, and ∑_j T_jj=Id_U.",["n","T","U"],[["i1","Fin(n)"],["j1","Fin(n)"],["k1","Fin(n)"],["l1","Fin(n)"]])]),
s("S003","Fix arbitrary r and temporarily assume L1: r≤ell. Then r<p. M003 gives red(r!) a unit, hence nonzero. N002 gives r! X_M(r)=x_M^r and r! Y_M(r)=y_M^r; N003 lets us apply F, preserving powers and integer multiples. Therefore F(X_M(r))=red(r!)^(-1)F(x_M)^r and F(Y_M(r))=red(r!)^(-1)F(y_M)^r. Discharge L1 and quantify r. The proof only inverts factorials with indices at most ell<p.",["M003","N002","N003","H001","H002","H003"],[],["r","ell","p","K","red","F","X_M","Y_M","x_M","y_M"],[f("F003","For every natural s≤ell, red(s!)≠0, F(X_M(s))=red(s!)^(-1)F(x_M)^s, and F(Y_M(s))=red(s!)^(-1)F(y_M)^s.",["ell","red","F","X_M","Y_M","x_M","y_M"],[["s","natural number"]])],["L1"],["L1"]),
s("S004","Let W be any K-linear subspace of U and temporarily assume L2: W is invariant under F(x_M),F(y_M). By induction it is invariant under every power of each operator, with the identity as the base. Linearity of W and F003 give invariance under F(X_M(r)),F(Y_M(r)) for all r≤ell. The factors in A_ij=X_M(ell−i)Y_M(ell)X_M(ell)Y_M(ell−j) all have indices between 0 and ell, so their F-images preserve W by composition and the ring-homomorphism laws. Finally multiplication by red(c_j)^(-1) preserves W because W is K-linear. Thus every T_ij preserves W. Discharge L2 and universally quantify W. Along with F001,F002 this proves N004; Lie invariance has never been used to infer stability of divided powers of index at or above p.",["N003"],["F001","F002","F003"],["W","K","U","F","x_M","y_M","X_M","Y_M","A","T","red","c","ell","n"],[],["L2"],["L2"])
],applications:[
ap("M003","S001","R0=K, p0=p, r0=ell.",["H001 states p is prime.","H002 gives characteristic p; H003 gives ell<p so the right-to-left implication yields a unit."]),
ap("M004","S001","n0=ell, j0=j.",["j∈Fin(n)=Fin(ell+1), hence j≤ell."]),
ap("M003","S003","R0=K, p0=p, r0=r, under r≤ell.",["H001 states p is prime.","H002 gives char K=p; H003 and L1 imply r≤ell<p, so M003 yields a unit."])
]});
rs.push({id:"R005",inputs:["M001"],output:"N005",definitions:[],rules:["direct","forall_introduction","implication_introduction","case_elimination","exists_elimination"],locals:[
l("k0","field","S001","S006","arbitrary","Fix an arbitrary field k0.",[]),
l("n0","natural number","S001","S006","arbitrary","Fix an arbitrary natural n0.",[]),
l("U0","k0-vector space","S001","S006","arbitrary","Fix a k0-vector space U0.",["k0"]),
l("T0","family Fin(n0)×Fin(n0)→End_{k0}(U0)","S001","S006","arbitrary","Fix a family of endomorphisms T0.",["n0","k0","U0"]),
l("W0","k0-linear subspace of U0","S001","S006","arbitrary","Fix a k0-linear subspace W0.",["k0","U0"]),
l("w0","vector in U0","S003","S006","witness","Choose w0∈W0, w0≠0, using F001.",["U0","W0"],[],["F001"]),
l("j0","Fin(n0)","S004","S006","witness","Choose j0 with T0_j0,j0(w0)≠0 using F002.",["n0","T0","w0"],[],["F002"]),
l("u0","vector in U0","S004","S006","definition","Put u0=T0_j0,j0(w0).",["U0","T0","j0","w0"]),
l("uFamily","family Fin(n0)→U0","S004","S006","definition","For each index i set uFamily_i=T0_i,j0(u0).",["n0","U0","T0","j0","u0"]),
l("acoef","family Fin(n0)→k0","S005","S005","arbitrary","Take arbitrary coefficients acoef_i.",["n0","k0"]),
l("kidx","Fin(n0)","S005","S005","arbitrary","Fix an arbitrary index kidx to extract its coefficient.",["n0"])
],argument:[
s("S001","Fix arbitrary k0,n0,U0,T0,W0. Temporarily assume L1: n0>0, dim_{k0} U0=n0, T0_ij T0_kl=T0_il if j=k and 0 otherwise, ∑_j T0_jj=Id_{U0}, and W0 is invariant under all T0_ij. These are precisely the antecedent data of the asserted theorem.",[],[],["k0","n0","U0","T0","W0"],[],["L1"],[]),
s("S002","Use the exhaustive cases W0={0} or W0≠{0}. In the zero case L3: W0={0}, the required disjunction follows immediately; discharge L3 for that branch. In the remaining branch assume L2: W0≠{0}. By the definition of a zero subspace there exists a vector in W0 different from 0.",[],[],["W0","U0"],[f("F001","There exists a vector w∈W0 with w≠0.",["W0","U0"],[],["L1","L2"])],["L3","L2"],["L3"]),
s("S003","Choose w0∈W0 nonzero using F001. Apply the diagonal-sum identity in L1: w0=∑_j T0_jj(w0). If every summand were zero, w0 would be zero. Hence there exists j∈Fin(n0) with T0_jj(w0)≠0.",[],["F001"],["w0","W0","T0","n0","U0"],[f("F002","There exists j∈Fin(n0) with T0_jj(w0)≠0.",["n0","T0","w0"],[],["L1","L2"])]),
s("S004","Choose j0 from F002 and put u0=T0_j0,j0(w0). Stability gives u0∈W0; it is nonzero by choice. The relation T0_j0,j0^2=T0_j0,j0 gives T0_j0,j0(u0)=u0. Define uFamily_i=T0_i,j0(u0). Every uFamily_i belongs to W0 by stability.",[],["F002"],["j0","w0","u0","uFamily","T0","W0","n0","U0"],[f("F003","u0≠0, u0∈W0, T0_j0,j0(u0)=u0, and uFamily_i∈W0 for every i∈Fin(n0).",["u0","W0","T0","j0","uFamily","n0"],[],["L1","L2"])]),
s("S005","Take arbitrary coefficients acoef and assume L4: ∑_i acoef_i uFamily_i=0. Fix kidx∈Fin(n0) and apply T0_j0,kidx. The multiplication law from L1 kills every term except i=kidx, yielding 0=∑_i acoef_i T0_j0,kidx T0_i,j0(u0)=acoef_kidx T0_j0,j0(u0)=acoef_kidx u0. Since k0 is a field and u0≠0 by F003, acoef_kidx=0. This holds for every kidx. Discharge L4 to prove linear independence of uFamily.",[],["F003"],["acoef","kidx","uFamily","T0","j0","u0","n0","k0","U0"],[f("F004","uFamily:Fin(n0)→U0 is k0-linearly independent.",["uFamily","n0","U0","k0"],[],["L1","L2"])],["L4"],["L4"]),
